DXSPIDER WEB INTEGRATION
========================

DXSpider supplies a native WebCluster interface used by two independent
reference applications: dxweb/ (user frontend) and dxweb-admin/ (administration
and supervision). DXSpider remains authoritative for command validation,
protocol processing and user management. Browser sessions do not require
individual traditional DXSpider network connections.

APPLICATIONS
------------
DXWeb: dxweb/app.pl; direct HTTP port 7380.
DXWeb Admin: dxweb-admin/admin.pl; direct HTTP port 7381.
Both connect through independent technical #WEB-n connections to the DXSpider
IntMsg listener, normally 127.0.0.1:27754 (TCP). The technical transport
is not an authenticated browser identity.

ACCESS MODES
------------
Without Nginx:
  Browser -> DXWeb :7380 or DXWeb Admin :7381 -> DXSpider :27754

With Nginx (examples in dxweb/docs/):
  Browser -> Nginx :7380 -> DXWeb 127.0.0.1:7480 -> DXSpider :27754
  Browser -> Nginx :7381 -> Admin 127.0.0.1:7481 -> DXSpider :27754

The application listener ports must be changed when enabling Nginx; do not
bind Nginx and an application to the same address and port. Use HTTPS for
public authenticated or administrative access. Never expose backend ports
7480/7481 or the DXSpider IntMsg listener to untrusted networks.

